WEBVTT

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:01.427
Because before following
my own dreams --

00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:03.304
being a filmmaker --

00:03:03.304 --> 00:03:04.388
I was a good daughter,

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:05.389
a good girl,

00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:06.974
and I followed my father’s dreams

00:03:06.974 --> 00:03:08.893
and I studied architecture and finished.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:16.067
And what I learned in architecture school
is how much you can learn about people,

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.068
about their story,

00:03:17.068 --> 00:03:20.863
about societies through the spaces
that they inhabit,

00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:21.906
through every object,

00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:23.783
every frame, every wall,

00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:24.784
through the ground,

00:03:24.784 --> 00:03:25.785
through the streets.

00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:27.119
But what do you do

00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:30.539
when you feel like the ground
on which you’re standing might not hold?